--
-- Test and training workspaces were indistinguishable from client work: many companies carry the same demo name and the
-- account home listed them all alike. A workspace's PURPOSE is now explicit, recorded metadata — never inferred from a
-- name, a code or an account number:
--   client    the company's own reporting
--   test      acceptance, demonstration or other testing
--   training  training
-- No recorded purpose means "not stated" (shown as such), never a default.
--
-- workspace_purpose_events is append-only (the latest event is in force; history is kept). Only the company's owner
-- records a purpose, with a reason, through set_workspace_purpose(); members with workspace access read it. Nothing about
-- a company, an engagement, an upload, a certification, a report version or a sealed pack is changed or deleted: purpose
-- is a label for the account home, and it gates nothing.

